{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.QArithmetic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.QArithmetic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.syt3_squares_sum_eq_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.syt3_squares_sum_eq_six","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L202-L207","doc":"Sum of `(d_λ)²` over partitions of `n = 3` equals `n! = 6`\n(Burnside / RSK identity).  `1² + 2² + 1² = 6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.syt3_dims","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.syt3_dims","kind":"def","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L198-L200","doc":"The standard-Young-tableaux dimensions `(d_[3], d_[2,1], d_[1,1,1])\n= (1, 2, 1)` for the three partitions of `n = 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qHookProduct_col3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qHookProduct_col3","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L193-L196","doc":"Hook product for the column `[1,1,1]` equals `[3]_q!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.hooksCol3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.hooksCol3","kind":"def","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L189-L191","doc":"Hook lengths for the column partition `[1, 1, 1]` of `n = 3`.\nCells: (1,1)→3, (2,1)→2, (3,1)→1.  Same multiset as `hooksRow 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qHookProduct_lshape21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qHookProduct_lshape21","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L182-L187","doc":"Hook product for `λ = [2, 1]` is `[3]_q · [1]_q · [1]_q = [3]_q`\n(since `[1]_q = 1` whenever `q ≠ q⁻¹`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.hooksLshape21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.hooksLshape21","kind":"def","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L178-L180","doc":"Hook lengths for the L-shape partition `[2, 1]` of `n = 3`.\nCells: (1,1)→3, (1,2)→1, (2,1)→1.  Returned in row-major order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qHookProduct_row_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qHookProduct_row_three","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L173-L176","doc":"Hook product for the row partition `[3]` equals `[3]_q!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qHookProduct_row_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qHookProduct_row_two","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L164-L171","doc":"Hook product for the row partition `[2]` equals `[2]_q · [1]_q\n= (q + q⁻¹) · 1`.  At `q = q_0 ≈ 1.11` this gives a positive\nvalue; the genuine Wenzl-bridge `dim_q([2])` is then\n`[2]_q!/H_q([2]) = (q+q⁻¹)/(q+q⁻¹) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.hooksRow_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.hooksRow_three","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L161-L162","doc":"For `λ = [3]` (single row of length 3), hook lengths are `[3, 2, 1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.hooksRow_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.hooksRow_two","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L158-L159","doc":"For `λ = [2]` (single row of length 2), hook lengths are `[2, 1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.hooksRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.hooksRow","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L153-L156","doc":"Hook lengths for the row partition `[n]` are `n, n-1, …, 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qHookProduct_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qHookProduct_cons","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L149-L151","doc":"The hook product distributes over `cons`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qHookProduct_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qHookProduct_nil","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L146-L147","doc":"The empty partition has hook product `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qHookProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qHookProduct","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L139-L144","doc":"The q-hook product `H_q(λ) = ∏_{x ∈ λ} [h_x]_q` over a partition\n`λ` represented as the list of its hook lengths.  The `dim_q(λ)`\nformula is `[n]_q! / H_q(λ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qFactorial_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qFactorial_two","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L133-L137","doc":"`[2]_q! = [2]_q · [1]_q = q + q⁻¹` (for `q ≠ q⁻¹`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qFactorial_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qFactorial_one","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L127-L131","doc":"`[1]_q! = [1]_q = 1` (for `q ≠ q⁻¹`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qFactorial_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qFactorial_zero","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L124-L125","doc":"`[0]_q! = 1` by convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qBinomial_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qBinomial_self","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L117-L122","doc":"`[n choose n]_q = 1` whenever `[n]_q!` is non-zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qBinomial_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qBinomial_zero","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L110-L115","doc":"`[n choose 0]_q = 1` whenever `[n]_q!` is non-zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qBinomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qBinomial","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L97-L108","doc":"**q-binomial coefficient** `[n choose k]_q := [n]_q!\n/ ([k]_q! · [n−k]_q!)`.  Note: this is the ratio definition;\nwhen `q − q⁻¹ ≠ 0` and the denominator is non-zero (always\ntrue at generic `q`) the result is a well-defined rational.\n\n**DEPRECATED duplicate (bean `5ldf` consolidation, 2026-06-26).** Bit-for-bit\nthe canonical balanced q-binomial `QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBinom`\n(the local `qInteger` ≡ that module's `qBracket`; verified). New code should use\nthe canonical one; kept here for the existing local consumers\n(`WenzlBridgeConcrete`, `GroundRingAnnotations`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qFactorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qFactorial","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L92-L95","doc":"The q-factorial `[n]_q! = ∏_{k=1..n} [k]_q`.  Returns 1 for n = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qInteger_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qInteger_succ","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L78-L90","doc":"**Recursion for q-integers**: `[n+1]_q = q · [n]_q + q⁻ⁿ`\nfor `q ≠ q⁻¹`.  Equivalently expanded as a sum of monomials,\n`[n]_q = q^(n-1) + q^(n-3) + … + q^(-(n-1))` (n terms).\n\nAlgebraic proof: using `qInteger q (n + 1) = (q^(n+1)\n− q⁻^(n+1))/(q − q⁻¹)`, one rearranges the numerator\n`q^(n+1) − q⁻^(n+1) = q · (q^n − q⁻^n) + q⁻ⁿ · (q − q⁻¹)`\nwhich yields the recursion after dividing by `q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qInteger_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qInteger_three","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L67-L76","doc":"`[3]_q = q² + 1 + q⁻²` for `q ≠ q⁻¹`.  Closed form of the\nthird q-integer; uses the factorisation `q³ - q⁻³ =\n(q - q⁻¹)(q² + 1 + q⁻²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qInteger_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qInteger_two","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L58-L65","doc":"`[2]_q = q + q⁻¹` for `q ≠ q⁻¹` — closed form of the second\nq-integer.  Used by the Markov-parameter substitution\n`z = 1/[2]_{q^{1/2}}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qInteger_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qInteger_one","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L53-L56","doc":"[1]_q = 1 for q ≠ q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qInteger_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qInteger_zero","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L49-L51","doc":"[0]_q = 0 for all q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qInteger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qInteger","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GaugeFieldFluidDynamics/QArithmetic.lean#L39-L47","doc":"The q-integer [k]_q = (q^k - q^{-k})/(q - q^{-1}). ","signatureChunk":0}]}